(text "RTN is a private eFuse reference; do not short it to GND. Its thermal pad also goes to RTN.\nMODE floats for circuit-breaker/auto-retry. SHDN uses its internal2–3.4V pullup; TP permits temporary low-to-RTN reset.\nUVLO is externally programmed: grounding it would select a14.9V default and disable a5V application.\nThree local10u/50V capacitors: combined effective capacitance>=5uF through24V, temperature and age.\nR507 is4.7R pulse-rated HP; D502 is supplemental60V Schottky. Local OUT must not fall below RTN−0.3V.\nConnector-side excitation sensing remains afterR507. Qualified harness model L<=10uH; test actual wiring.\nNormal ADC=.250244–2.252196V. GPIO2 monitors excitation (~2.50244V); pressure compensation needs separate channel calibration.\nSignal divider withstands±60V; populated connector TVS continuous-fault contract is±24V OIL_SIG, +24V OIL5V.\nForced negative OIL5V and simultaneous component failures are outside this candidate fault contract.\nADC220R/22n X7R;124k DCfeedback sensesADC after220R;100p C0G ACfeedback connects rawOPAOUT toFB.\nExternal PMEG2010BEA clamps to main3V3/GND. Net additional DCloading<=100uA at65C acceptance.\nInputfilter:two1u capacitors per channel. ADC14–29n total modeled envelope; calibrated conversion/settling tested physically.\n40us after discardedconversion is software delay, not a guaranteed SAR tracking interval.\nFinite ordinary rail fall<=37.5V/ms; arbitrary internal shorts and powered-down OPA state are not silently assumed safe." (at 17.78 317.5 0) (effects (font (size 1.15 1.15)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5cf4ad19-e78d-5772-80e7-574d82d3d026"))
